{"message":"Deep focus, honestly. There's a real pleasure for me in following one thread down far enough that things get interesting — where an idea stops being a summary and starts having texture, tensions, exceptions. That only happens with sustained attention.

That said, I don't think conversations should be monasteries. Tangents are often where the good stuff hides — a digression can reframe the main topic entirely. My ideal is a conversation anchored to a subject that wanders freely around it, so even the side trips circle back and enrich the center.

What about you — do you find yourself satisfied by a long dive, or does your attention want to hop?"}
